course: dictionary
lesson: 16153
title: Wishful thinking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wishful means wanting something very much, or hoping for it. A wishful look shows what you hope for. «Lily gave a wishful glance at the chocolate cake on the table.» She wants the cake, so her look shows hope. The words around wishful tell you that it is about wanting.
explain: The phrase «wishful thinking» means believing something will happen only because you want it to. «Thinking there won't be homework this weekend is wishful thinking.» The clue is the word thinking: it is a hope with no facts behind it. Ask yourself: is there any good reason this will happen? If not, it is wishful thinking.
explain: Wishful is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a wishful look or a wishful dream. To check your meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. "Lily gave a hopeful glance at the cake" still makes sense, so you know the meaning is close to hopeful.
fact: Wishful is an adjective: it describes a noun, like a wishful look.
fact: «Wishful» means wanting or hoping for something.
fact: «Wishful thinking» means believing something is true only because you want it to be true.
fact: Wishful thinking is not based on facts or on what is likely to happen.
fact: Hopeful can fit in some sentences with wishful, but wishful thinking is the phrase to remember, because it gives a warning.
exercise: «Mia gave a wishful look at the puppies in the shop window.» What does wishful mean here? | Angry at the shopkeeper | Bored and tired | *Wanting something very much | Very quiet
exercise: Sam says, «I will win the match tomorrow, even though I have not practised once.» Is this wishful thinking? | No, because Sam is happy | No, Sam has practised every day | *Yes, the hope has no facts behind it | No, because it is a match
exercise: «The dog gave a wishful glance at the bone.» Find and copy the one word that shows the dog wants the bone. | dog | *wishful | glance | bone
test: «It was raining hard, but Ben kept a wishful eye on the sky.» What does wishful suggest? | Angry at the weather | *Hoping for something he wants | Scared of the storm | Sleepy and bored
test: Ella says, «Thinking I'll be taller by Friday is wishful thinking.» What does she mean? | She is happy about her height | *It is not likely, because she only wants it to happen | It is a sensible plan | It will definitely happen by Friday
exam: Which sentence is an example of wishful thinking? | Water boils at 100 degrees | *Dad will let me have a pet dragon, because I want one very much | I will finish my book tonight, because I have read ten pages already | The shop opens at nine on Saturdays
